    function setUp() public { c = new C(); }
    function testFuzz_property(address lrtConfigAddr) public {
        // The admin role check is on the lrtConfig contract. Since we cannot mock it,
        // we need to first set a valid lrtConfig that gives admin role to someone.
        // However, the bug is in updateLRTConfig which is only callable by LRTAdmin.
        // LRTAdmin checks the DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE on the current lrtConfig contract.
        // If lrtConfig is address(0), the external call to IAccessControl(address(lrtConfig)).hasRole(...) will
        // succeed on an EOA (return false) and revert with CallerNotLRTConfigAdmin.
        // To call updateLRTConfig, we need an lrtConfig that returns true for hasRole(DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE, msg.sender).
        // We deploy an adversarial helper that returns true for the admin role check.
        AdminGranter granter = new AdminGranter();
        // First, initialize C with the helper's address as lrtConfig so that the initial lrtConfig is set.
